---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Fixture from "../../components/Fixture.astro";
---
<Base title="Badge" description="iVOLT badge: small status labels with subtle and solid colour variants. CSS only.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Badge</h1>
    <p>A compact label for status or counts. Badges are not interactive; if the label matters to assistive technology, keep it as real text, not colour alone.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/badge.css</code> (in <code>ivolt.css</code>).</p>
    <Fixture name="badge/variants" />
    <h2>Classes</h2>
    <p><code>iv-badge</code> plus <code>--primary --success --warning --danger --info</code> (subtle background, coloured text) and <code>--solid</code> (filled). Without a variant the badge is neutral.</p>
    <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul><li>Using a badge as a button; use <code>iv-button--sm</code> instead.</li><li>Conveying state by colour only: include a word such as “Paid”.</li></ul>
  
    <h2>Class index</h2>
    <p>Parts and modifiers of this family that the examples above do not show. The full list per stylesheet lives in the <a href="/reference">reference</a>.</p>
    <div class="docs-scroller docs-class-index">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>iv-badge--primary</code></td><td>Primary tone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>iv-badge--info</code></td><td>Informative tone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>iv-badge--success</code></td><td>Success tone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>iv-badge--warning</code></td><td>Warning tone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>iv-badge--danger</code></td><td>Danger tone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>iv-badge--solid</code></td><td>Filled variant: the tone becomes the background instead of the tint.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
